{
  "requirement": "Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through\ntheir `ValidationContext`. The application supplies the configuration under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`. The SDK does not persist it.\nA cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the reviewed tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through their `ValidationContext`.\n2. The application supplies the configuration through `ValidationCache::with_agent` (cited, so only its use here is checked).\n3. The SDK does not persist the configuration.\n4. A cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria (cited `deterministic_procedures`).\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Obligation 1, agent obtained from the cache.**\n  - `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` builds a `TestDomain` whose cache comes from `ValidationCache::with_agent(OpenAiConfig{..})`. It runs `validation::verify` twice. A local HTTP server receives four requests, and the test asserts the model, the tool list, the prompt and the returned answer. The criterion therefore reached the cache-selected agent through the validation context.\n  - `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` does the same for the Ollama backend. It also asserts the endpoint, the bearer key and the options in the request.\n  - `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` covers the failure path. An awaited ask on a cache with an unusable credential fails with `ValidationError::Agent`, and the error names the environment variable.\n  - `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` calls `verify_with_agent` with an explicit agent. It adds isolation coverage but is not needed for this obligation.\n- **Obligation 2, the config is attached to the cache.** `bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted` checks that the cache holds the same agent (`Arc::ptr_eq`) across domain clones and that `agent.config` equals the supplied config. It also checks that the new cache is otherwise empty.\n- **Obligation 3, not persisted.**\n  - The Bedrock test serializes the stored evidence record. It asserts there is no `backend` key and that neither the profile string `development` nor `claude-sonnet` appears.\n  - The OpenAI test makes the same check after each `store_evidence`. The saved JSON must not contain the API key, the model name, `backend` or `api_key`.\n  - Together these check both the secrets and the backend settings.\n- **Obligation 4, a cache without an agent supports deterministic criteria.**\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` uses `Memory`, whose cache is the default one with no agent. An ask returns `ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured`. A deterministic `Review` criterion verifies and stores evidence with the expected dependency.\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` adds a check that a missing agent stores nothing.\n  - `new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent` in `domain.rs` shows the default cache has `agent.is_none()`.\n  - The converse case, deterministic criteria on a cache that has an agent, is also covered. In `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors`, a deterministic refresh leaves `agent.provider.get()` as `None`, which shows backend setup is deferred. It also records one dependency and a correct output.\n- **Supporting check.** `supported_backend_settings_create_transports_without_sending_requests` shows that each backend configuration can build a transport without sending a request.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found no unacknowledged gap. Each obligation has a test that exercises it and asserts its outcome.",
